      "math_academy_id": "q-224995",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(9)$ given below, find the value of $P(X\\le 7).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.0212\\,$ | $\\,0.0550\\,$ | $\\,0.1157\\,$ | $\\,0.2068\\,$ | $\\,0.3239\\,$ | $\\,0.4557\\,$ | $\\,0.5874\\,$ |",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 7) & =F(7) \\\\  & =0.3239.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
